<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<ScrollView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@color/bg_deep"
    android:fillViewport="true"
    android:scrollbars="none">

    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:orientation="vertical"
        android:paddingLeft="20dp"
        android:paddingRight="20dp"
        android:paddingTop="18dp"
        android:paddingBottom="24dp">

        <!-- ══════════ header: brand centered, gear beside the brand ══════════ -->
        <RelativeLayout
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content">

            <!-- The brand line and the settings control share this row, so the
                 control is centred on "Quant of Rehan" itself rather than on
                 the brand block with its tagline (owner order 2026-10-13), and
                 it is centred on that line vertically as well, owner order
                 2026-10-14 below. The tagline sits below the row and never
                 influences the control. -->
            <RelativeLayout
                android:id="@+id/brand_row"
                android:clipChildren="false"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content">

                <!-- The brand face (owner order 2026-10-12): Bonskin, the
                     owner's own script signature face, at 30sp.
                     No letterSpacing and no textStyle="bold": tracking a
                     script face breaks its joins, and Android would fake a
                     bold from a face that already carries one weight.
                     30sp is measured, not guessed: the string advances
                     6.677 em, so 200dp on the narrowest phone this app
                     supports, against about 320dp of content width.

                     includeFontPadding stays at its default (true) for the
                     same measured reason: Bonskin's ink for this exact string
                     reaches 779/1000 em while its TYPOGRAPHIC ascender is only
                     730/1000, so the tighter box would shave the top of the
                     capital Q. The default box uses the font's hhea metrics
                     (1006 / -288), which contain the ink with room to spare. -->
                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/brand_title"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_centerHorizontal="true"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/bonskin"
                    android:gravity="center"
                    android:paddingBottom="2dp"
                    android:shadowColor="@color/crimson_logo"
                    android:shadowDy="2"
                    android:shadowRadius="6"
                    android:text="@string/app_name"
                    android:textColor="@color/gold_bright"
                    android:textSize="30sp"/>

                <!-- The settings control (owner order 2026-10-13): the owner's
                     own settings.png silhouette (res/drawable-nodpi/
                     settings.png, 512x512, a black gear on transparency,
                     copied from his Desktop byte for byte), tinted into the
                     app's palette and sitting on no plate at all. The old gear
                     vector and its two plates are retired. The open state is
                     the quarter turn and the brighter gold, both done in
                     MainActivity.setSettingsOpen, and its only background is a
                     masked circular ripple, so a press is acknowledged without
                     a tile ever being drawn.

                     Owner order 2026-10-13 (second note): the control stands
                     ON the brand line's baseline rather than centred on the
                     row. It is anchored to the title here, and MainActivity
                     puts its bottom edge on the title's own baseline once the
                     layout exists, because that line's position comes from
                     Bonskin's metrics and from the system font scale and
                     cannot be expressed as a fixed margin.

                     Owner order 2026-10-13 (third note): the control used to
                     overflow its row, because its box is 42dp tall while a
                     30sp Bonskin line stands only about 30dp of ink above its
                     baseline. The row therefore turns clipChildren off, so
                     the guarantee does not rest on one magic number once the
                     system font scale moves that line.

                     Owner order 2026-10-13 (fourth note): the control stands
                     directly BESIDE the title instead of pinned to the row's
                     far edge, so it is always next to "Quant of Rehan" and
                     never floating alone in the corner. It is anchored with
                     layout_toEndOf the title, which keeps the pair together
                     at any screen width and at any font scale: the icon
                     measures from the title's own right edge, so the title can
                     never grow into it. The 6dp left margin plus the
                     control's own 6dp padding leave 12dp of air between the
                     name and the ink, the grid's own unit and the same 12dp
                     the rules use.

                     Owner order 2026-10-14 (sixth note): the control is
                     VERTICALLY CENTRED on the title. The baseline rule of the
                     second note is retired: standing the box on the brand
                     baseline needed a measurement after every layout, because
                     Bonskin puts its baseline wherever its metrics and the
                     system font scale say, and a 42dp box hung on that line
                     sat low against the name. centreVertical in the row the
                     title and the control share puts the box's own middle on
                     the title's middle, so the pair reads level at any font
                     scale with no measured pixel and no layout listener at
                     all. -->
                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/btn_settings"
                    android:layout_width="42dp"
                    android:layout_height="42dp"
                    android:layout_centerVertical="true"
                    android:layout_toEndOf="@id/brand_title"
                    android:layout_marginLeft="6dp"
                    android:background="@drawable/settings_ripple"
                    android:contentDescription="@string/cd_settings"
                    android:padding="6dp"
                    android:scaleType="fitCenter"
                    android:src="@drawable/settings"
                    android:tint="@color/gold"/>
            </RelativeLayout>

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/brand_tagline"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_below="@id/brand_row"
                android:layout_centerHorizontal="true"
                android:layout_marginTop="4dp"
                android:fontFamily="@font/lemonmilk_light"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:letterSpacing="0.18"
                android:text="@string/tagline"
                android:textColor="@color/teal"
                android:textSize="10sp"/>
        </RelativeLayout>

        <!-- brand rule: line, diamond, line (from the logo frame). Defined
             once in layout/qor_rule.xml and included at each of the four
             divisions: under the header, between the system status and the
             latest signal tiles, after the signal tile, and after the market
             tile, so "the same as the ones above" is true by construction. -->
        <include
            layout="@layout/qor_rule"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="12dp"/>

        <!-- ══════════ system status card ══════════ -->
        <LinearLayout style="@style/QorPanel"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="16dp"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <TextView style="@style/QorLabel"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:text="@string/label_system"/>

            <!-- Owner order 2026-10-11: the state is a status light plus the
                 word, in one badge. The indicator is a vector drawable and
                 MainActivity swaps it with the state, so ONLINE and OFFLINE
                 are the same shape lit and unlit rather than two glyphs.

                 Owner order 2026-10-14 (seventh note): the beacon is its own
                 view now, not a compound drawable of the word. A compound
                 drawable can only be animated by rewriting its bounds and
                 alpha from the UI thread, which is the lag the owner
                 reported; as a view, the pulse is an alpha and scale
                 animation the platform interpolates on the render thread.
                 The badge stays one pill: the beacon and the word are its
                 two children, and the word keeps the face, the size and the
                 colour that carry the state. The beacon keeps its 18dp.

                 Owner order 2026-10-14 (eighth note): the air above this
                 badge is @dimen/status_gap, exactly the gap the detail line
                 below it uses, so the tile reads SYSTEM STATUS, ONLINE,
                 KARACHI at one spacing rather than at two. -->
            <LinearLayout
                android:id="@+id/status_pill"
                android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_gravity="center_horizontal"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/status_gap"
                android:accessibilityLiveRegion="polite"
                android:contentDescription="@string/cd_status_checking"
                android:gravity="center_vertical"
                android:importantForAccessibility="yes"
                android:minHeight="34dp"
                android:orientation="horizontal"
                android:paddingLeft="16dp"
                android:paddingRight="16dp"
                android:paddingTop="5dp"
                android:paddingBottom="5dp">

                <ImageView
                    android:id="@+id/status_dot"
                    android:layout_width="18dp"
                    android:layout_height="18dp"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:src="@drawable/ic_status_checking"/>

                <TextView
                    android:id="@+id/status_word"
                    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginLeft="@dimen/status_dot_gap"
                    android:fontFamily="@font/lemonmilk_bold"
                    android:importantForAccessibility="no"
                    android:letterSpacing="0.08"
                    android:text="@string/status_checking"
                    android:textSize="13sp"/>
            </LinearLayout>

            <!-- Owner order 2026-10-13: every line in this tile is set in the
                 owner's faces, so the detail keeps QorValue (LEMON MILK
                 Light) instead of the system face. The clock span no longer
                 forces monospace inside the tile either.

                 Owner order 2026-10-14 (eighth note): the air above this
                 line is the same @dimen/status_gap the badge uses, so the
                 tile's spacing is one number: SYSTEM STATUS to ONLINE is
                 ONLINE to KARACHI, exactly. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/status_detail"
                style="@style/QorValue"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="@dimen/status_gap"
                android:gravity="center"/>

        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- Owner order 2026-10-13 (second note): a rule divides the system
             status tile from the latest signal tile, so every change of
             subject on the console is marked. The same include as the others,
             so the diamond is the logo's and is defined once. -->
        <include
            layout="@layout/qor_rule"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="12dp"/>

        <!-- ══════════ latest signal card ══════════ -->
        <LinearLayout style="@style/QorPanel"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="12dp"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <TextView style="@style/QorLabel"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:text="@string/label_signal"/>

            <!-- The same order sets this tile's lines in the owner's face. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/signal_list"
                style="@style/QorValue"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="8dp"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:text="@string/no_signals"/>
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- brand rule after the latest signal: the same include, closing the
             card section like the logo frame -->
        <include
            layout="@layout/qor_rule"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="18dp"/>

        <!-- ══════════ settings (hidden until the gear is tapped) ══════════ -->
        <LinearLayout
            android:id="@+id/settings_panel"
            style="@style/QorPanel"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="14dp"
            android:orientation="vertical"
            android:visibility="gone">

            <TextView style="@style/QorLabel"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:text="@string/label_settings"/>

            <TextView style="@style/QorBody"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="6dp"
                android:text="@string/settings_hint"/>

            <EditText
                android:id="@+id/token_box"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="10dp"
                android:background="@drawable/field_bg"
                android:hint="@string/token_hint"
                android:inputType="textVisiblePassword"
                android:padding="12dp"
                android:textColor="@color/text_bright"
                android:textColorHint="#FF6E5A78"
                android:textSize="12sp"/>

            <LinearLayout
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="10dp"
                android:orientation="horizontal">

                <Button
                    android:id="@+id/btn_save"
                    style="@style/QorButton"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:text="@string/btn_save"/>

                <Button
                    android:id="@+id/btn_open"
                    style="@style/QorButton"
                    android:layout_width="0dp"
                    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                    android:layout_marginLeft="8dp"
                    android:layout_weight="1"
                    android:text="@string/btn_relay"/>
            </LinearLayout>

            <Button
                android:id="@+id/btn_arm"
                style="@style/QorButton"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="8dp"
                android:text="@string/btn_arm"/>
        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- ══════════ market card ══════════
             Third box, same shape as the two above: KSE100 points and
             percentage plus the day's top three KMIALL stocks by volume,
             rebuilt by the relay every five minutes.

             Owner order 2026-10-12: the card carries no "MARKET NOW" label
             any more. The index line and the ranking state what the card is
             by themselves, and the label was the last piece of chrome the
             owner asked to have removed. -->
        <LinearLayout style="@style/QorPanel"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="14dp"
            android:orientation="vertical">

            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/market_index"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="10dp"
                android:fontFamily="@font/lemonmilk_bold"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:text="@string/market_waiting"
                android:textColor="@color/text_bright"
                android:textSize="17sp"
                android:textStyle="bold"/>

            <!-- The card's values carry LEMON MILK Light (QorValue): tickers,
                 money and counts are capitals by nature, so the free face's
                 uppercase-only mapping costs nothing here. The up and down
                 arrows are the exception and are drawn with the system face
                 by a span in MainActivity, because no bundled face has
                 U+25B2/U+25BC. -->
            <TextView
                android:id="@+id/market_leaders"
                style="@style/QorValue"
                android:layout_width="match_parent"
                android:layout_height="wrap_content"
                android:layout_marginTop="8dp"
                android:gravity="center"
                android:text="@string/market_leaders_waiting"/>

        </LinearLayout>

        <!-- Owner order 2026-10-13 (second note): the diamond rule that used to
             close the third tile from inside it now stands immediately after
             that tile's own boundary, so the divider reads between the card
             and the air below it rather than as part of the card. It is the
             same include, with the same diamond, as the three above.

             Owner order 2026-10-13 (third note): the cadence sentence leaves
             the market card and stands immediately after this final diamond
             rule. Owner order 2026-10-13 (fifth note): the sentence is
             separated from the rule by the layout's own 12dp, the same gap
             a tile has below its rule, so the console's last line sits on
             the same grid as everything above it. The two leading newlines
             the third note used are retired: the air above the sentence is
             now a margin the grid can measure, while the sentence itself
             stays exactly as ordered and still appears exactly once in the
             whole app. -->
        <include
            layout="@layout/qor_rule"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="12dp"/>

        <!-- The cadence line, 12dp below the last rule: the same gap the
             signal tile has below its own rule, so the footer's spacing is
             the grid's spacing. It is a caption like the card's other small
             print, and it is the last element of the console: no footer rule
             follows it (owner order 2026-10-12). -->
        <TextView
            android:id="@+id/scan_cadence"
            style="@style/QorCaption"
            android:layout_width="match_parent"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginTop="12dp"
            android:gravity="center"
            android:text="@string/scan_cadence"/>
    </LinearLayout>
</ScrollView>
